# chat-transcript
- label: the chat transcript is proven live in a real browser: a served run whose stub agent writes growing claude-format JSONL renders the user bubble, thought marker, "Explored 2 searches" grouping, and human tool titles, then renders the appended events (including an Edit file card with +N/-N stats) without a reload while chat polling stays active — and a run that never writes a recording shows the pending state (skips cleanly without playwright/tmux)
  id: cupw
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'chat transcript' test/browser/run-watch.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, tests, implemented]

# chat-composer
- label: the composer is proven in a real browser against a live run: typed text submits via Enter AND via the round send button (data-empty flips as text is typed and clears), the keys popover opens with all six keys and a clicked Enter reaches the agent's tty as a bare Enter while the menu closes and focus returns, the agent chip opens the run-details popover (agent/run-id rows, Stop-vs-Kill-run note, honest "detecting…" model row with the chip hidden while no recording reports a model) mutually exclusive with the keys menu and Escape-closable, a session-writing run unhides the model chip with the shortened session-reported model and links the recording row to /view, and the status strip's Stop control C-c-interrupts the run to the exited state with the strip swapping to "Agent exited" and the card retiring (skips cleanly without playwright/tmux)
  id: cmpw
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'composer send paths|composer Stop control|chat transcript renders appended' test/browser/run-watch.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-composer, ui, tests, implemented]
- label: the in-composer run feedback is proven in a real browser against a live run: while the stub session holds an unresolved tool call the strip text becomes the humanized live action (not 'Running') with data-busy=true and the empty-input send button morphed to the stop control; typing flips the button back to a queue-labeled send whose Enter HOLDS the message as a visible queue row ('1 in queue', input cleared, nothing typed into the pane) with a second message counting '2 in queue'; x removes a row, clicking a row's text pulls it back into the input, 'send now' types a queued row into the agent's terminal immediately; and once the stub completes its turn and the recording goes quiet the remaining queue auto-delivers in order into the pane and the queue block empties (skips cleanly without playwright/tmux)
  id: cmfw
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'in-composer state feedback' test/browser/run-watch.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-composer, ui, tests, implemented]

# app-integration
- label: the integrated flow is proven in a real browser — from the dashboard the "+ New run" button opens the launcher modal listing the stub agent, Start lands directly on /run?id=<id> with the chat header showing the run; back on the dashboard the run appears as ONE first-class run row in the main session list (running state badge, launch prompt, activity line, no strip row or chat badge anywhere else) and clicking the row returns to the chat; the row's kill control dismisses the run; with tmux absent the modal shows the missing-multiplexer state; and GET /launch redirects to the dashboard launcher (skips cleanly without playwright/tmux)
  id: cipw
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/browser/launch-ui.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-integration, ui, tests, implemented]
